    "Medium": [
      {
        "context": "The manifest checks run before make_snapshot() and therefore before producer validation, but report() does not consistently convert manifest and fixture identity failures into its stable JSON failure contract. A missing manifest raises FileNotFoundError at digest(); syntactically malformed manifest JSON raises JSONDecodeError at load(); a missing required fixture and a renamed required fixture are both detected as fixture-manifest-binding by validate_fixture_set(), then report() unconditionally invokes run_fixture_set_meta_counterexamples(), whose current.pop(target) raises KeyError. All four variants fail closed and never reach producer validation, so this is not a false green. However, the verifier emits a traceback instead of an auditable truth-test-failed report for these exact drift classes.",
        "file": "measure/tracks/apk_existing_asset_candidate_audit_20260712/phase4_global_contract_test.py",
        "id": "P4G-M-01",
        "lines": [
          500,
          536,
          537,
          541,
          544
        ],
        "required_remediation": "Catch missing/unreadable/invalid-JSON manifest failures as fixture-manifest-binding, and when manifest_errors is non-empty either skip meta-counterexample execution against the invalid inventory or make every meta mutation defensive. The CLI must return exit 1 plus structured truth-test-failed JSON for missing manifest, malformed manifest JSON, missing required fixture, and renamed required fixture. Add durable tests for all four variants without changing the required manifest identity.",
        "severity": "Medium",
        "title": "Four manifest and fixture identity failures traceback instead of returning structured fail-closed JSON"
      }
    ]
  },
